  response:
  - No actually it goes like this
  - I'm standing in the garage of my grandparents house at night. I'm looking out
    with my feet frozen in place
  - I see headlights coming up the driveway and the garage door opens automatically.
    It's like a jaw. It's dripping and the sound it makes is like growling
  - That's when I start to feel afraid. The headlights are coming towards me like
    eyes and they're growling too but above them I can see an illuminated windshield
    and the faces of my grandparents
  - They're looking right through me. Totally expressionless. They're going to hit
    me and I scream at them
  - The jaws of the garage slam shut and in the darkness I feel the car roll over
    me slowly from head to toe.
  - I don't wake up. It crushes me. I feel my bones grind against each other. I feel
    the air forced out of my lungs
  - Type shit
  - Didn't break a sweat texting you
  - And for good reason. Weird ass answer
  - Bye sweet dreams
